@startuml
!theme plain
title Catalog 3 of 3 · Like and low-stock notification
autonumber
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true

actor "Customer" as U
actor "Manager" as MG
participant "Frontend" as F
participant "NestJS API" as A
database "PostgreSQL" as DB
queue "Redis / BullMQ" as Q
participant "Worker" as W
participant "SMTP" as M

== Liking a product ==
U -> F : Taps the heart
F -> A : PUT /products/ID/like\nliked true
activate A
alt No token
  A --> F : 401 Unauthorized
else Caller is a manager or courier
  A --> F : 403 Forbidden
  note right of A : A manager can't like a product:\nthis isn't a bookmark, it's a subscription
else The product doesn't exist
  A --> F : 404 NotFound
else Success
  A -> DB : Registers the subscription
  A --> F : 200 liked true
end
deactivate A

== What triggers the notice ==
MG -> F : Restocks or corrects stock
F -> A : PATCH /skus/ID
A -> DB : Updates the stock
note right of A : A sale triggers it too:\nany write that leaves the variant\nat the low-stock threshold

alt The variant drops to the low-stock threshold
  A -> Q : Queues the low-stock notification
  Q -> W : Delivers the job
  W -> DB : Product subscribers
  note right of W : Only to whoever has **never** paid for that product.\nWhoever already bought it doesn't need the notice
  loop for each recipient
    W -> M : Sends the notice with the specific variant
  end
else Still above the threshold
  note right of A : Nothing is queued
end

note over Q, W
  Three attempts with backoff and then the failed queue.
  Losing a stock notice is recoverable; that's why
  this queue doesn't have the payment-settlement policy.
end note

@enduml
